# goal Reject ambient browser and DNS-rebinding input before agents run

This module is the request-front boundary for Host, Origin and inference media
types. It reduces unauthenticated browser exposure; it is not authentication and
must never be documented as one.

`readJsonBody` owns the 32 MiB inference-body bound and OpenAI-shaped JSON parse
errors used by the extracted handlers.

# rule Validation sources

Host authority comes only from the configured listener, the accepted socket's
local address, or `server.allowedHosts`; never trust forwarded headers. Origin is
same-origin or explicitly allowed by `server.cors`. `cors: true` is the operator's
explicit wildcard, including opaque origins. Chat/Responses POST endpoints accept
only `application/json` with an optional UTF-8 charset.

# invariant Validation precedes model work

`validateHttpIngress` runs before body parsing, registry lookup, session admission,
agent spawn or prompt. Failures are OpenAI-shaped through `RequestError`: 400
`invalid_host`, 403 `invalid_origin`, or 415 `unsupported_media_type`.

# test HTTP ingress

- wrong Host, foreign Origin and text/plain inference are rejected before open
- same-origin browser requests work without CORS response headers
- explicitly allowed CORS and proxy/Docker host names remain usable
- MCP POST and body-less GET/DELETE routes are not misclassified as inference
